# W30c, b (k10), a stranger to a and c: the gate to stag0201 twice. First c's row (Here (1)) above a's, the cursor on c's:
# B (the first answer of autochoice back,first). After c went home: only a's row (nobody of it at stag0201), the cursor on
# New instance; the first row is taken: b enters stag0201 as a guest in a new stage group of a's instance.
campaign until stage=stagml11,control
idle until epoch>=@220
explore mate00 until onme:mate00
gate mate00 1 until frames>=150
log b went back
idle until epoch>=@320 fail stage=stag0201
explore mate00 until onme:mate00
gate mate00 1 until stage=stag0201,control
log b a guest at stag0201
idle until frames>=180
disk 8 until stage=stagml11,control
log b home
